1 0 0 1 60 680 Tm (The road north climbs out of the valley before dawn.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 665 Tm (Trucks pass in convoys, headlights cutting the fog.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 650 Tm (By mid-morning the pass is a ribbon above the clouds.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 635 Tm (Everything that travels this route is counted twice.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 620 Tm (The convoy halts for the border check at noon.) Tj
1 0 0 1 290 581 Tm (Soldiers wave the drivers) Tj
1 0 0 1 290 567 Tm (through without ceremony.) Tj
1 0 0 1 290 553 Tm (The paperwork travels ahead,) Tj
1 0 0 1 290 539 Tm (by fax, to the next post.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 455 Tm (By evening the column reaches the northern plain.) Tj
1 0 0 1 60 440 Tm (The drivers sleep in the cab, engines idling.) Tj
